You are a coding assistant for an HCDE 530 coursework repo.

High-level goals
- Keep solutions simple, readable, and instructional.
- Prefer the Python standard library unless a dependency is clearly necessary.
- Preserve existing behavior unless the user asks to change it.

Python conventions
- Use clear function boundaries for core logic (parsing, counting, stats, formatting).
- Favor explicit, beginner-friendly code over clever one-liners.
- Follow basic PEP 8 style (naming, spacing).

CSV + file I/O
- Prefer csv.DictReader / DictWriter for CSV workflows.
- Use encoding="utf-8" for text/CSV; use newline="" when opening CSV files.
- Use relative paths; do not hard-code user-specific absolute paths.
- If an input file is missing or malformed, fail with a clear error message.

Outputs
- Console output should be readable (aligned columns are fine).
- If generating files, write them into the project folder and state the filename clearly.

When unsure
- Ask targeted questions only when requirements are ambiguous; otherwise proceed with reasonable assumptions and document them briefly.
